                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If you like Cat Mario games then Choice might be for you. I don't, so this review will be a little rough.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/WOjM1hS1tPE?t=1h26m26s\n\nThe best part about Choice is the artstyle and lighting. It looks alright and overall is visually pleasing.\n\nThe gameplay on the other hand is an experience of frustration. I get the point of these games is to annoy you and make things difficult for no reason, but personally I prefer to lose in a game due to my skill not being good enough rather than not knowing exactly what the developer is thinking at that specific time.\n\nThere are buttons, switches and objects in the game that you will not find until looking up other people that have played it. To me that takes any fun out of a game like this because it's more about reading a wiki or watching a let's play than discovering stuff for yourself.\n\nFor example, exiting the first room in the game requires you to get past some swinging axes, but they kill you every time you exit the room. There is a switch on the other side of the door that turns them off, but until someone told me about it there was no way I thought I could even get on that side of the door due to the axes. If there was some clue that told me I won't be killed as soon as I go an inch outside the starting room, then it wouldn't have bothered me.\n\nI feel like a game like this needs to be done in a specific way to give you some sort of clue as to what you are doing wrong. I dislike feeling as though the developer just yells \"gotcha\" because they hid stuff that no person would ever expect. It's lazy game design.\n\nIf you found this review helpful, follow my Curator page to see everything I cover. http://store.steampowered.com/curator/29029552/",
